  "term": "aversion conditioning",
  "definition": "Aversion conditioning is a form of learning in which a stimulus becomes rejected because it is paired with something unpleasant or aversive. In the source packet, it refers to using an unpleasant consequence alongside appetitive conditioning to strengthen discrimination learning.",
